CLASS:Rogue Knight	HD:10	TYPE:Prestige.PC	STARTSKILLPTS:2	MAXLEVEL:10	CSKILL:Bluff|TYPE=Craft|Diplomacy|Disguise|Gather Information|Hide|Intimidate|Knowledge (Nobility and Royalty)|TYPE=Profession|Ride|Sense Motive	BONUS:COMBAT|BASEAB|classlevel	BONUS:SAVE|Fort|CL/2+2	BONUS:SAVE|Ref|CL/3	BONUS:SAVE|Will|CL/3	AUTO:WEAPONPROF|TYPE=Simple|TYPE=Martial	AUTO:ARMORPROF|ARMORTYPE=Light|ARMORTYPE=Medium|ARMORTYPE=Heavy	AUTO:SHIELDPROF|SHIELDTYPE=Shield	DESC:Knights cast out of their orders. Ex-Solamnic and dark knights (Table 1-17, Former Knight Levels, p.44) gain by their former knighthood levels: 1-2 hardhearted (Su, a morale bonus equal to Charisma bonus on saves against fear and despair); 3-4 +2 on Bluff, Listen, Sense Motive, Spot and Survival against members of the former knighthood and +2 initiative against them in combat (Ex); 5-6 fate's hand (Su, Charisma modifier as a morale bonus on all saves, and smite law once a day: + Charisma to attack, +1 damage per rogue knight level against a lawful foe); 7-8 another +2 on those skills and initiative; 9 or more: Solamnic or dark knight prestige levels are traded one for one for rogue knight levels (Rose or Thorn first, then Sword or Skull, then Crown or Lily), and traded levels do not count for these abilities. Honor-Bound is a Dragonlance Campaign Setting feat: turn that book on.	PRETEXT:Martial Weapon Proficiency (any one)	PRETEXT:Was a member of an order of knighthood (such as the Order of the Crown or Order of the Lily), and broke or betrayed an oath as described under Honor-bound and required atonement (completing it is not required)	PREBAB:5	PRECHECKBASE:1,Fortitude=4	PREFEAT:1,Armor Proficiency (Heavy)	PREFEAT:1,Honor-Bound	SOURCEPAGE:p.43-44
